# Impulse Unit Tests

## Basic impulse values
impulse1 = 100 newton-seconds
# Expected: 100 newton-seconds

impulse2 = 50 pound-force-seconds
# Expected: 50 pound-force-seconds

## Impulse conversions (the NASA Mars Climate Orbiter scenario)
converted1 = 100 newton-seconds in pound-force-seconds
# Expected: 22.48

converted2 = 100 pound-force-seconds in newton-seconds
# Expected: 444.82

## Impulse arithmetic
total = 50 newton-seconds + 50 newton-seconds
# Expected: 100 newton-seconds
